# Domain clarification gate

Bob often ships domain UI via Cursor without a written eng spec. **Do not invent
bowling tournament rules, pot UX, lock behavior, or counting semantics in the client.**

## Before implementing domain-affecting UI

If ambiguous, **ask 2–5 concrete questions first** (examples over prose). Do not
build large UI until answered or a named safe default is agreed.

| Ambiguity | Ask with an example |
|-----------|---------------------|
| Who counts | “8 tickets, 5 unique bowlers — standings rows show how many?” |
| Lock | “After lock, which buttons stay enabled?” |
| Scope | “Pool picker: per squad vs all squads?” |
| Window | “Games 1,2,4 — show non-contiguous checkboxes?” |
| Live vs process | “Standings from GET only, or still calling process/calculate?” |
| Reports | “Which report menus are in-scope for this ship?” |

## Safe defaults

Match an existing pot type’s UI patterns and backend capability matrix. State the
default in one line. Never invent a client-only counting rule.

## Never silently invent

- Client engines / projections that disagree with backend  
- Name-keyed maps for domain logic  
- Keeping retired `calculate*` / `process*` clients “for later”
